infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Performance discipline vs crisis mode
  desc Same org, two cultures — the gap is 15–30 points of engineering capacity, freed permanently
  compares
    - label With discipline
      children
        - label 5–10% eng-time on perf
          desc Steady-state, mostly proactive maintenance
        - label Toil under 30%
          desc Gates and runbooks absorb the repetitive work
        - label ~50% lower infra bill
          desc 2× throughput halves the cloud cost for that workload
        - label Incidents drop 50–70% in Q1
          desc Near-zero for known failure classes after 12 months
        - label Compounds, survives turnover
          desc Accumulated CI gates are inherited on day one
    - label Crisis mode (no discipline)
      children
        - label 20–40% eng-time on perf
          desc Reactive firefighting, not product work
        - label Toil 70–80%
          desc Page-out, manual triage, fix, repeat in 3 months
        - label Full cloud bill
          desc Scale by adding machines, no throughput headroom
        - label 2–3 SLO-burning incidents/quarter
          desc 20–40 engineer-days consumed each
        - label Same failures recur
          desc The same root cause returns every 3–6 months
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
